1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:05,036
In this simulated branch, an approved request leaves the backend.

2
00:00:05,386 --> 00:00:07,481
The reply never arrives.

3
00:00:08,581 --> 00:00:10,030
Did the change fail?

4
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:12,087
Or did only the reply fail?

5
00:00:12,787 --> 00:00:16,144
The SQLite ledger already says CALLING.

6
00:00:16,444 --> 00:00:18,142
It was committed before the call.

7
00:00:18,742 --> 00:00:22,596
So AWSOps does not send that write again.

8
00:00:22,896 --> 00:00:26,371
It reconciles the same run, read-only.

9
00:00:26,971 --> 00:00:32,071
A matching S3 policy, independently read back, answers one question only.

10
00:00:32,571 --> 00:00:34,917
Execution is still unknown.

11
00:00:35,117 --> 00:00:37,101
Compliance is unknown.

12
00:00:37,301 --> 00:00:39,416
Freshness is not verified.

13
00:00:39,716 --> 00:00:42,470
No AWS Config evaluation has run.

14
00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:47,961
Until the missing evidence is resolved, the outcome stays NEEDS_REVIEW.

15
00:00:48,561 --> 00:00:52,214
This demonstrates control logic, not live acceptance.
